CC Desk
Uses SwiftTerm (MIT License) by Miguel de Icaza and contributors: https://github.com/migueldeicaza/SwiftTerm
Uses WhisperKit (MIT License) by Argmax, Inc.: https://github.com/argmaxinc/argmax-oss-swift

Screen detection rules (Sources/CCDeskCore/BundledManifests.swift: codex.toml, pi.toml) and the
event mapping of the Codex hook / pi extension are derived from herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr),
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
The manifests are included unmodified; the hook script and extension were rewritten for CC Desk.

Release builds embed tmux (ISC License, https://github.com/tmux/tmux) at Contents/Helpers/tmux, statically
linked with libevent (3-clause BSD License, https://libevent.org) and utf8proc (MIT License,
https://github.com/JuliaStrings/utf8proc). Their full license texts are in
Contents/Resources/ThirdPartyNotices/tmux.txt.

Color themes adapt the published palettes of Catppuccin (MIT), Rosé Pine (MIT), Everforest (MIT),
Tokyo Night (Apache-2.0), Solarized (MIT), Gruvbox (MIT) and Nord (MIT); some colors are adjusted for
contrast. Sources are listed in docs/specs/2026-10-02-cc-desk-design.md.

Downloaded on demand at runtime (not bundled): the Whisper large-v3 turbo CoreML model
(argmaxinc/whisperkit-coreml, MIT), and for the optional natural voice, mlx-audio (MIT) and
Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice (Apache-2.0).
